AUDIO: 'Deepseek just released a dedicated vision model and it\'s incredibly cheap coming in as low as 0.00008 cents per photo, meaning you can run this at scale behind your own apps and services. Today we\'ll test out how'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'capable this really is in real world conditions. [music] We\'ll snap foods, labels, random objects outside to see how well the model performs. I took about 14 photos as part of the test and it cost me less than 1 P. So, let\'s see'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'how good Deep Seek Vision really is. So, just a quick rundown of how this works before we jump into the tests.'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Vision is available under the model name DeepS V4 Flash Vision EXP. The EXP being experimental. Deepsee it themselves say the model accepts images alongside text. So, you can ask the model to describe'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pictures, read text from screenshots, analyze charts, and more. We can send images in three ways. First, as a base 64 encoded image as part of the standard request body. However, the encoded data counts towards the 48 megabyte request'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'body limit. So, this will only work for smaller images. The second option is you can provide an external image URL. But here, the image can be maxed 32 megabytes and the download must complete within 60 seconds. And the final option'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is file upload via the files API. This lets you send larger images and it\'s likely the option you\'d want and what I\'ll be using for my demos today. Now, it\'s also worth noting smaller images are scaled up to reach roughly 384x 384'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pixels and larger images are scaled down to match roughly 800x 800 pixels. I say roughly because the aspect ratio is always preserved. This can mean that'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'small details and text could be lost before the model even had a chance to read them. So, just something to keep in mind. And with that said, let\'s go take some photos. But before we do, you do me a huge favor by subscribing to the channel so we can keep bringing you'

[01:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
